    <p>{`XMLHttpRequest objects are used to interact with servers.
You can retrieve data from a URL without having to do a full page refresh.
This enables a Web page to update just part of a page without disrupting what the user is doing.`}</p>
    <p>{`In order to leverage `}<inlineCode parentName="p">{`XMLHttpRequest`}</inlineCode>{`, update the `}<inlineCode parentName="p">{`manifest.json`}</inlineCode>{` with the `}<inlineCode parentName="p">{`network.domains`}</inlineCode>{` permission shown in the example section`}</p>
    <b> Example </b>
    <pre><code parentName="pre" {...{
        "className": "language-json"
      }}>{`{
  "permissions": {
      "network": {
          "domains": [
              "https://www.adobe.com",
              "https://*.adobeprerelease.com",
              "wss://*.myplugin.com"
          ]
      }
  }
}
`}</code></pre>
    <b>Limitation:</b>
From UXP v7.4.0 onwards `permissions.network.domains` does not support WildCards in top-level domains. Example:
    <pre><code parentName="pre" {...{
        "className": "language-json"
      }}>{`"domains": [ "https://www.adobe.*", "https://www.*" ]
`}</code></pre>
